\DOC SIMPS_CONV

\TYPE {SIMPS_CONV : thm list -> conv}

\SYNOPSIS
Simplify a term with the simp set and some more theorems.

\DESCRIBE
{SIMPS_CONV thl tm} simplifies {tm} with the rules that have been
declared with {add_simp}, with the theorems of {thl} on top of them, and
with HOL Light's built-in simplifications. It is {SIMPLIFY_CONV (simp_ss
()) thl}, so it is conditional contextual rewriting and everything
{SIMP_CONV} says applies.

\FAILURE
Fails if the term cannot be simplified, as {SIMP_CONV} does.

\EXAMPLE
{
  # SIMPS_CONV [ADD_CLAUSES] `count (Call (Cons (Num 3) Nil))`;;
  val it : thm = |- count (Call (Cons (Num 3) Nil)) = 1

  # SIMPS_CONV [] `Num 3 = Call Nil`;;
  val it : thm = |- Num 3 = Call Nil <=> false
}

\SEEALSO
add_simp, SIMP_CONV, simp_ss, SIMPS_RULE, SIMPS_TAC.

\ENDDOC
